    <string name="path_explain_bluetooth">The iPhone starts CarPlay over Bluetooth, and Carlink finds the car over Bluetooth.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_hotspot">The iPhone, and a car using the browser, join this hotspot. Its name and password must match the relay settings, or the iPhone cannot join.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_car_network">The car reaches this phone over its hotspot or the same Wi-Fi, not over Wi-Fi Direct.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_car_page">The first time, the browser warns about the certificate: choose Advanced, then Proceed.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_carplay_start">CarPlay starts after the car, so it uses the car\'s real screen size and does not restart.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_bluetooth_off">This phone\'s Bluetooth is off. Turn it on; CarPlay continues by itself.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_iphone_unpaired">The iPhone is no longer paired with this phone. Pair it again in the iPhone\'s Bluetooth settings.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_rfcomm_timeout">The iPhone did not answer over Bluetooth. Keep it near and unlocked, with Bluetooth on.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_wifi_off">Wi-Fi is off on this phone. Turn it on and try again.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_wifi_reset_required">Android\'s Wi-Fi Direct is stuck. Turn Wi-Fi off and on again, then retry.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_usb_trust_denied">The iPhone did not trust this phone. Plug it in again and tap Trust.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_iphone_locked">Unlock the iPhone; CarPlay then continues.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_usb_role">With a USB-C to USB-C cable the iPhone becomes the USB host and this phone cannot see it. Use a USB-C OTG adapter with a USB-A cable.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_carlink_blocked">Carlink and CarPlay over Wi-Fi Direct cannot run together. Choose the phone hotspot.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_web_port_busy">Another app uses this port. Close it, or change the port in Developer settings.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_auth_rejected">The car did not accept this phone. Retry and enter the code shown on the car.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_peer_key_changed">The car\'s key changed (reset, or another car). Pair again with the code.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_projection_timeout">The car did not start the picture in time. Keep Carlink in front and retry.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_heartbeat_timeout">The link to the car dropped. It reconnects by itself; keep Carlink open on the car.</string>
    <string name="path_explain_wifi_join">This phone could not join the car\'s Wi-Fi. Keep Wi-Fi on and Carlink open, then retry.</string>
